It's no trouble at all to level up after buying
protection in Mines Town and in the process after
that of sacrificing for an eventual artifact. Level
three is trivial to reach, because while you're
raising your level you're making newly generated
monsters higher level too, at half the pace. I just
did a game (unsuccessful like all of mine) where I
bought 8 points of protection in Mines Town, and
then leveled up to XL:9 before I left Mines Town.

Thus, your memory of arriving at XL:1 and also
getting Grayswander for sacrificing is perfectly
believable, you probably just didn't notice that
you'd leveled up in the process of acquiring
and using sacrifice material after getting cheap
protection.

xanthian.

With a _lot_ of help from lucrative bones files and
industrious credit cloning in perhaps seven or eight
shops between the main dungeon and Mines Town, I
once got to Mines Town at XL:1 with sufficient
zorkmids to do about 25 offerings. That gave me my
normal 9 protection points, plus two more
"difficult" protection points from beating the odds
on getting a "selfless generosity" response twice,
giving me a naked AC of -1.

Now if I could only manage to take advantage of such
good fortune early in the game.


